# — local / build state (never tracked) —
node_modules
.tmp/
REVIEW_*.md
.codegraph/
__pycache__/
vitest-report.json

# — .pi: the TOOLS are tracked for contributor parity; session state stays
# local. Any NEW .pi state dir is ignored by default. —
.pi/*
!.pi/skills/
!.pi/extensions/

# — .pi/brl-subagent: the project-local presets and templates ARE the dispatch
# contract (they take precedence over the shipped copies at dispatch time), so
# they are tracked (#514) — otherwise a clean checkout dispatches a different
# text than this one. Extension state (`state.json`, …) stays local: the `/*`
# line re-ignores every child of the directory, and the negations below re-admit
# only the contract files. A NEW contract file must be tracked: the tracking
# check (`scripts/check-contract-tracking.mjs`) fails on an untracked one. —
!.pi/brl-subagent/
.pi/brl-subagent/*
!.pi/brl-subagent/*.md
!.pi/brl-subagent/presets/
!.pi/brl-subagent/templates/

# NOTE: .development/ is tracked deliberately (#247). It was untracked in
# b134db4 (2026-07-26) together with the graph-snapshot bloat; #247 restores
# the documentation half.
